INSERT INTO moments (id, place_id, slug, title, body, date_start, date_display, date_precision, hero_media_id, status) VALUES ('00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000d0d8', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000b0b1', 'twin-city-zephyr-crash', 'The Twin-City Zephyr Crash', 'On April 3, 1947, the Twin-City Zephyr passenger train collided with a tractor near the Main Street station in Downers Grove. The tractor had fallen from a freight car moving on an adjacent track. The collision killed two passengers and a train-service employee. The Interstate Commerce Commission''s investigation also recorded injuries among passengers and several members of the train crew.

The Zephyr was approaching Chicago from Minneapolis when the accident occurred. The local Historical Society describes the locomotive catching fire, the first two coaches jackknifing and the station being severely damaged. The event placed a long-distance passenger service, a freight movement and the village''s everyday station in the same chain of consequences. The site was recognized through the Historical Society''s historic-sites program in 1997.

The federal investigation reached a specific conclusion about cause. Its report, dated May 26, 1947, attributed the accident to freight being operated with a load that was not properly secured. That finding is more precise than describing the wreck simply as a collision at a station. The tractor was freight in transit, and its movement out of a freight car created the obstruction encountered by the passenger train. The commission investigated alongside a representative of the Illinois Commerce Commission.

The report places the collision at about 10:40 p.m. in misting weather. The passenger train was moving east on one track and the freight train west on the adjacent track. Investigators recorded that a signal displayed a proceed indication as the passenger train approached. The fireman saw the obstruction and called a warning as the engineer moved the brake valve to emergency. The locomotive and cars derailed, and coaches struck the station area. These recorded details show how quickly an unsecured load on one train endangered people on a neighboring track, even within a signal-controlled railway.', '1947-04-03', 'April 3, 1947', 'day', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000f0f1', 'published');

